-- §10b Every `between` as a reference to another document, beside whether it lands on a layer here.
# One row per filed reference, with the filing its notation resolves to, or the typed reason it
# resolves to nothing.
#
# Reported, not asserted
#   A part reference that dangles is a violation, and `checks/unresolved_part.sqlc` says so,
#   because a fusion sum cannot be worked out without it. A `between` that dangles is ordinary, and
#   the schema says so among the element's own refusals: a group eliminating against a member that
#   files nothing, or against a layer folded into a different composed layer, is ordinary, and a
#   keyref forcing the subset would make the honest case impossible to file. Writing the part
#   rule's shape here would accuse a filing the model names as correct.
#
# Nothing else brings it into view
#   *A rule reads only what it needs*, so the thing that normally makes a reference a named object
#   is the check that reads it. `between` is the one reference to another document no rule may
#   check, so without this query it would stay a raw table, read as evidence for a number rather
#   than as a pointer at another document.
#
# A general gap, not one about eliminations
#   Anything the model licenses but no rule may judge is invisible to queries that grow by rules.
#   Observations are the answer, and this is one.
-- eliminations/references.sqlc against eliminations/resolved.sqlc, the whole beside the half.
SELECT a.composition                        AS "composition!",
       a.composed_layer                     AS "composed_layer!",
       a.quantity::text                     AS "quantity!",
       a.party                              AS "party!",
       a.layer                              AS "layer!",
       coalesce(r.resolved_filing, '(outside this corpus)') AS "lands_on!",
       (r.resolved_filing IS NOT NULL)      AS "resolves!"
FROM      (
    :compose(eliminations/references.sqlc)
) a
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(eliminations/resolved.sqlc)
) r USING (composition, composed_layer, quantity, seq)
ORDER BY (r.resolved_filing IS NOT NULL), 1, 2, 3, a.seq
